Done. One file changed: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts` (+223, −0).

**What it does**
- `refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter` now calls `ensureCommandVecTableForDim(database, active.dim)` right beside `ensureVecTableForDim`.
- New `readCommandEmbeddingSources()` resolves `command-bridges.generated.json` through two candidates (source `runtime/lib/skill-graph` → `runtime/scripts/…`, dist → `runtime/scripts/…`, mirroring `route-exclusions.ts`). Missing/unparsable/wrong-shape returns `null`, so the skill refresh still completes.
- New `refreshCommandEmbeddings()` runs after the skill loop: same `computeContentHash` skip rule (hash + `model_id` both match ⇒ no embed call), same `modelId = active.name` column, same dim mismatch guard, same 3-failure outage streak (seeded from the skill loop's outage so a proven-dead backend is not asked again), same delete-on-failure write. Prunes command ids the projection no longer names, since `command_id` has no foreign key.
- Legacy path and the skill loop body are unchanged. `SkillEmbeddingRefreshResult` has no natural field for command counts and folding them into `embedded`/`skipped`/`failed` would misreport the skill corpus, so they are logged the way the function logs today: `[skill-graph] Command embeddings: N embedded, N skipped, N failed, N pruned` (plus `COMMAND-BRIDGES-UNAVAILABLE` / `COMMAND-EMBEDDING-FAILED` / `COMMAND-EMBEDDING-BACKEND-OUTAGE` prefixes).

